==English==
[[File:Mate en calabaza.jpg|thumb|maté]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|mate<id:drink>}}
* {{alt|en|matë<l:rare>}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|es|mate|id=drink}}, from {{der|en|qu|mati}}.<br/>
Here, as well as in the {{m|en|matë}} variant, the [[unetymologically|unetymologically]] accented ''e'' serves the purpose in English of marking that vowel as pronounced, as in {{m|en|latte}}, rather than silent as in {{m|en|mate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmæteɪ/|/ˈmɑteɪ/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-maté.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|æteɪ|s=2|ɑːteɪ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[evergreen]] [[tree]], {{taxfmt|Ilex paraguariensis|species}}, native to [[South America]], cultivated for its leaves.
#: {{syn|en|yerba mate|yerba}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[beverage]], resembling [[tea]], made from the dried leaves of this plant.
#: {{syn|en|maté tea}}
#: {{ux|en|We spent a month in Buenos Aires drinking nothing but '''maté''' and Fernet with soda.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A cup of this drink.
# {{lb|en|countable|uncommon}} The [[container]] used to prepare this drink, traditionally a small [[calabash]].
#: {{syn|en|gourd}}
#: {{cot|en|bombilla}}

